{"name":"Arctic Dawn","hex":"#e3e5e8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arctic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Arctic."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Arctic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arctic"},{"term":"dawn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To begin to brighten with daylight.","To start to appear or become obvious."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The morning twilight period immediately before sunrise.","The rising of the sun."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dawn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arctic","blocks":[{"text":"The Arctic is the polar region of Earth that surrounds the North Pole, lying north of the Arctic Circle. The Arctic region, from the IERS Reference Meridian travelling east, consists of parts of northern Norway, northernmost Sweden, northern Finland, Russia, the United States (Alaska), Canada, Danish Realm (Greenland), and northern Iceland, along with the Arctic Ocean and adjacent seas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Arctic_%28orthographic_projection_with_highlights%29.svg/330px-Arctic_%28orthographic_projection_with_highlights%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic","wikidata":"Q25322"},{"title":"Dawn","blocks":[{"text":"Dawn is the time that marks the beginning of twilight before sunrise. It is recognized by the appearance of indirect daylight being scattered in Earth's atmosphere, when the centre of the Sun's disc has reached 18° below the observer's horizon. This morning twilight period will last until sunrise, when direct daylight outshines the diffused light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Desert_Dawn.jpg/330px-Desert_Dawn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawn","wikidata":"Q11326182"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Arctica_surface.jpg/500px-Arctica_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Arctica_surface.jpg/500px-Arctica_surface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArctica_surface.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg/500px-Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg/1280px-Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg/500px-Sunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunny_Skies_over_the_Arctic_in_Late_June_2010.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Aerial_photograph_Greenland_2023-10-14-3.jpg/500px-Aerial_photograph_Greenland_2023-10-14-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Aerial_photograph_Greenland_2023-10-14-3.jpg/1280px-Aerial_photograph_Greenland_2023-10-14-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Aerial_photograph_Greenland_2023-10-14-3.jpg/500px-Aerial_photograph_Greenland_2023-10-14-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pars